ss domain-based rate limiting (e.g., http://evil.com@legitimate.com).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"file\": \"src/api/routes.py\",\n      \"line\": 64,\n      \"description\": \"No authentication or authorization on any REST endpoints. Any user can query all historical queries, feedback, and system data without authentication.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"file\": \"src/api/websocket.py\",\n      \"line\": 76,\n      \"description\": \"Missing CSRF protection and rate limiting on WebSocket endpoint. No token validation, no request rate limits. Vulnerable to abuse and amplification attacks.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"file\": \"src/main.py\",\n      \"line\": 69,\n      \"description\": \"Sensitive API key checks logged as warnings. GEMINI_API_KEY exposure in error messages could reveal authentication requirements to attackers.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"file\": \"src/data/db.py\",\n      \"line\": 19,\n      \"description\": \"Hardcoded database path without encryption: SQLite database stores all queries, responses, and user feedback in plaintext. No field-level encryption for sensitive data.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"file\": \"src/main.py\",\n      \"line\": 36,\n      \"description\": \"Server binds to 0.0.0.0:8000 with no HTTPS enforcement. No HTTP Strict-Transport-Security header. Vulnerable to man-in-the-middle attacks in network transit.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"file\": \"src/main.py\",\n      \"line\": 27,\n      \"description\": \"Missing security headers: No Content-Security-Policy, X-Content-Type-Options, X-Frame-Options, or X-XSS-Protection headers configured.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"file\": \"src/api/routes.py\",\n      \"line\": 177,\n      \"description\": \"Unrestricted export endpoint: /feedback/export returns all feedback with no pagination, rate limiting, or authentication. Could expose large datasets.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"riskScore\": 72,\n  \"recommendations\": [\n    \"IMMEDIATE (High Priority):\",\n    \"1. Fix CORS: Change allow_origins=['*'] to specific origins. Remove allow_credentials=True or use more restrictive domain list.\",\n    \"2. Add input validation: Implement query length limits (e.g., max 5000 chars), validate WebSocket messages, use Pydantic validators.\",\n    \"3. Sanitize prompts: Never interpolate user input directly. Use parameterized prompt templates with {placeholder} substitution.\",\n    \"4. Add authentication: Implement JWT or session-based auth for all REST endpoints and WebSocket connections.\",\n    \"5. Remove error details: Catch exceptions, log details server-side, return generic error messages to clients (e.g., 'An error occurred').\",\n    \"6. Use proper URL parsing: Replace string.split() with urllib.parse.urlparse() or furl library for URL validation.\",\n    \"7. Add rate limiting: Use slowapi or similar library to limit requests per IP (e.g., 100 req/min for REST, 10 msg/min for WebSocket).\",\n    \"\",\n    \"SHORT TERM (Within 1-2 weeks):\",\n    \"8. Add HTTPS enforcement: Configure SSL/TLS, set HSTS header, force redirect from HTTP.\",\n    \"9. Security headers: Add middleware for CSP, X-Content-Type-Options, X-Frame-Options, Referrer-Policy.\",\n    \"10. Database encryption: Encrypt SQLite database at rest, add field-level encryption for sensitive columns (query_text, findings).\",\n    \"11. Audit logging: Log all access attempts, authentication failures, and sensitive operations with timestamps and user identifiers.\",\n    \"12. Input length limits: Set max_connections limit on WebSocket, validate query_text length before processing.\",\n    \"13. CSRF protection: Implement CSRF tokens for state-changing operations.\",\n    \"\",\n    \"LONG TERM (Within 1 month):\",\n    \"14. API key management: Move GEMINI_API_KEY to secure vault (AWS Secrets